#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Afterstreet parks pack, version 1 (26 October 2026): what a park, a playing field, a pool, a camp and a bike park hold: playground equipment, park furniture (shelters, fountains, statues, lamps, fences), baseball, basketball, tennis, soccer, football, volleyball and track pieces with court and line tiles, a skate park, a swimming pool with its fittings, golf pieces, a bike park (jumps, berms, a pump track), and tents and camp pieces.
Writes assets/shaped/parks.js. Run: python3 assets/shaped/src/parks.py

models.parks.<name>: metres, origin at the centre of the base, front facing +Z; pieces along a path or edge are 4 m long on z and tile end to end. Court, track and line tiles are 4 m decals at y = 0.02 (`court_*`, `track_*`, `field_line_*`); the pool sinks below y = 0 (its info has `sunk`), so cut the ground under it. `info[name]` has `note`, `use`, `holds` (what a search can find), `powered` and `water` as in the business packs."""
